# Skill: Remove AI Marks

Purpose:
  Multi-vendor AI provenance-mark removal skill: invisible Unicode (Layer A),
  statistical text watermarks via rewrite (Layer B), C2PA/EXIF/XMP/container
  metadata on PNG/JPEG/WebP/SVG/PDF/DOCX/ODT/HTML/MD. Thin-client skill —
  all deterministic cleaning runs in a separate Docker HTTP service.

Owns: ./

Source: https://github.com/guillaumemeyer/watermarks-remover
Origin: tmp/watermarks-remover/skills/remove-ai-marks/
Imported: 2026-09-06
Format: anthropic-skill (adapted to .sdd)
License: MIT
Runtime: docker (HTTP service via curl at 127.0.0.1:8765 — wr-core)
Provenance: this repo is already service-integrated via @sdd-purge.sdd (Layer A/B bridging)

ReadOrder:
   1  @INDEX.sdd
   2  @SKILL.md
   3  @references/mark-classes.md
   4  @references/removal-matrix.md
   5  @references/ethics.md

Modes:
  APPLY    — remove marks from owned files (via service)
  AUDIT    — detect marks without modification
  REVIEW   — inspect a file's provenance surface

Rules:
  [RAM1] This skill is a THIN CLIENT — cleaning machinery runs in the Docker HTTP service.
  [RAM2] Never run cleaning scripts directly on the host ([R59]-[R66]).
  [RAM3] Layer A (metadata/Unicode) allowed for owned files; Layer B (statistical rewrite) gated.
  [RAM4] Always offer Layer B, but apply only with explicit user intent.
  [RAM5] Use only for files the user owns or is authorized to process.

Entry:
  Read:
    INDEX.sdd
    SKILL.md

  Resolve:
    references/ethics.md
    references/how-claude-marks.md
    references/mark-classes.md
    references/markdiffusion.md
    references/removal-matrix.md
    references/vendor-notes.md

Navigation:
  RemoveAIMarks: @INDEX.sdd
  Skill: @SKILL.md
  MarkClasses: @references/mark-classes.md
  RemovalMatrix: @references/removal-matrix.md
  PurgeCommand: @../../commands/sdd-purge.sdd

State: +
